  "notes": "Paper presents sensitivity PROJECTIONS (kappa=2, ~95% CL, 3-year exposure) for reactor neutrino experiments (MINER, CONUS, CONNIE, nu-cleus) on BOTH the ALP-photon coupling g_agamma and the ALP-electron coupling g_aee (Fig. 3 top/bottom). Per pre-analysis hint, AxionElectron is selected, but the paper equally emphasizes AxionPhoton. No numerical limit values are given in tables or text \u2014 all projected curves are only in Fig. 3, which cannot be digitized from the text. Qualitative info: g_aee projections are flat for ma << 1 MeV (roughly 1e-6 to 1e-5 level based on axis range description), covering ma ~ 10 eV to ~few MeV; g_agamma flat limit for ma <= 1e4 eV with peak sensitivity near ma ~ 4 MeV. No data points extractable, hence low extraction confidence. Not a dark-matter search (reactor ALP production), so no DM density assumption. | vector-trace candidate: electron_limits_with_astro.pdf colour (0.86, 0.08, 0.24), 86 pts (selected among 7) | selector: vector_trace (sole candidate)",
